From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 15:25:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 230/342] meson_vdec: MJPEG, with linux-firmware's
 gxl_mjpeg.bin

Baseline JPEG pictures written one after the other, as Amlogic's driver
starts its MJPEG firmware (docs/m51-mjpeg-facts.md): four frames, its
list of free frames, the picture's height, the picture scaler at one to
one; reports in AV_SCRATCH_9 and _A, frames given back through _8.

The firmware writes three planes whatever MDEC_PIC_DC_NV12 says, so the
frames are planar 4:2:0 (meson_vdec_frame's new cr_offset); a 4:2:2
picture comes out 4:2:0 too, its chroma filtered. It decodes a picture
once more data follows: each picture is written with 4 KB of zeros after
it, and its frame comes right away.

On a C920's pictures: Y within 1 of libjpeg-turbo's, the chroma within
0.25 on average (the 2x2 mean of its 4:2:2); 10.8 ms a 1280x720 picture,
21.4 ms a 1920x1080 one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
